+**Token-state pages (UX §8.5 verbatim + truthful mapping; all render the site header/footer, no dead ends):**
+
+| State | Copy |
+|---|---|
+| Unknown token (404) | `This link doesn't look right. If you were expecting a reference form, the link may have been replaced by a newer one. Check the most recent message from us, or contact us: {/contact link}.` |
+| Expired, check still open | `This link has expired.` / `Links last 10 days so old messages can't be reused. If you still want to give this reference, we can send a fresh one.` / [ `Send me a new link` ] (POST form button) |
+| Resend success | `On its way. We've sent a fresh link to the contact details on file. It expires in 10 days.` |
+| Already completed (`form_completed`, `partial`) | `This reference was already completed. Thank you.` |
+| Declined (`refused`, `objected`) | `This reference was declined. No further messages will come from us.` |
+| Landlord handling (`manual_recorded`, `unreachable`, `failed`, `awaiting_correction`, taken-over + expired) | `The landlord is handling this reference directly. You don't need to do anything here.` |
+
+### The as-stated data-availability matrix (disk-truth deviation — verify, don't assume)
+
+UX §6.5 presumes the application captures previous-tenancy dates and rent. **Disk truth (verified 2026-08-08):** `application` has NO tenancy-date or tenancy-rent columns; it carries `employer_name`, `job_title`, `employment_duration` (a duration string, "How long in current role?"), `monthly_income_cents` (NOT NULL), and `current_address`. Architecture §5.3's own question list is open-first ("Did they rent from you? From when to when? / What was the monthly rent?"), so the open rendering is the sanctioned fallback.
+
+| Check | UX presumption | Disk truth | rc3-3 renders |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Landlord tenancy period | as-stated from→to | no columns | OPEN: month-year pair + ongoing (Q4) |
+| Landlord rent | as-stated €X/month | no column | OPEN: amount + don't-remember (Q5) |
+| Employer period | as-stated | `employment_duration` (nullable duration string) | as-stated DURATION check when present, open text when absent |
+| Employer role | as-stated `{job_title}` | `job_title` nullable | as-stated when present, open text when absent |
+| Employer salary | as-stated €/year | `monthly_income_cents` NOT NULL | always as-stated (annualised ×12) |
+
+`as_stated` truth in the result is rc3-4's structuring concern; the draft shapes above carry what it needs. **Flagged for the reconciliation pass:** UX §6.5's landlord Q4/Q5 wording assumes data the apply form never collects.
+
+### Token-state classifier (pure function — the heart of the handler)
+
+`classify(row: Option(FormContext), now: Timestamp) -> TokenState` — unit-test the full matrix:
+
+| row | status | taken_over | expired | → TokenState |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| none (unknown token) | — | — | — | `Unknown` → 404 unknown page |
+| any | `contact_initiated` | no | no | `Live` (landing / question / review) |
+| any | `contact_initiated` | yes | no | `Live` (A7: link survives takeover; resend NOT offered) |
+| any | `contact_initiated` | no | yes | `ExpiredOpen` → expired page WITH resend |
+| any | `contact_initiated` | yes | yes | `LandlordHandling` |
+| any | `form_completed`, `partial` | — | — | `Completed` |
+| any | `refused`, `objected` | — | — | `Declined` |
+| any | `manual_recorded`, `unreachable`, `failed`, `awaiting_correction` | — | — | `LandlordHandling` |
+| any | `queued`, `skipped` | — | — | unreachable (token never minted pre-T0) → `Unknown` |
+
+Expiry: `form_token_expires_at != '' AND now() > form_token_expires_at`. A NULL/empty expiry on a live row is treated as NOT expired (defensive — the sweep always stamps it; never lock a referee out on a data gap).
+
+### The resend flow (AC5 — writer semantics vs AD-14)
+
+1. `POST /reference/:token/resend` arrives only from the expired-open page's button (honeypot + timing apply).
+2. Guarded remint (new SQL `remint_form_token.sql`): `UPDATE reference_call SET form_token = $2, form_token_expires_at = now() + interval '10 days' WHERE form_token = $1 AND status = 'contact_initiated' AND taken_over_at IS NULL AND form_token_expires_at < now() RETURNING id, application_id, ref_slot, contact_name, contact_email, contact_phone, corrected_email, corrected_phone` — 0 rows = the state moved under the referee; re-render the current-state page (fresh classify).
+3. Send `send_invite` (rc3-2) to the EFFECTIVE contact (`COALESCE(corrected_*, contact_*)`, AD-7) with `base_url = domain_helpers.origin_from_domain(vacancy.origin_domain)` (the apply-canonical precedent; join vacancy in the context query).
+4. Audit: new `AuditEvent` variant `ReferenceCallLinkResent` → `"reference_call_link_resent"`, `entity_type: "reference_call"`, details carry the per-channel outcomes — NEVER the token (the `audit_log` row shape is a load-bearing contract: append-only new variant, no rename).
+5. Render the resend-success page.
+
+**Rate-limit by construction:** the remint bumps the expiry, so a second resend POST with the old token 404s (token dead) and one with the new token fails the `expired` guard — repeat resends are impossible without reading the fresh email. No attempt-log append: the sweep owns `attempts` (AD-14/§4.1) and the warm-handoff's "we messaged them N times" honestly counts sweep sends; the audit row is the resend evidence. (Rejected: attempt-log append without `attempt_count` bump — an uncounted attempt entry corrupts the cadence math the sweep derives from the log. Flagged for review.)
+
+### Route registration checklist (AC1 — the Perkins r1 fix)
+
+- `middleware.redact_token_route`: add `["reference", ..] -> Ok("/reference/<redacted>")` (prefix match covers `/answer` + `/resend`; CSP-report `redact_token_url` inherits the arm).
+- `middleware.is_public_path`: add `["reference", ..] -> True` (covers the token + sub-paths; the apply/dsar/erase POST precedent — public POSTs carry no CSRF token by design).
+- Router: the five arms in the route table above, placed with the other public SSR arms BEFORE the SPA catch-all; the `http.Get, ["reference", ..]` catch-all is what keeps typo'd deep links off the SPA shell (AC7).
+- Regression tests in `server/test/middleware/middleware_test.gleam` for both middleware arms (mirror the dsar/erase pins: `sentry_safe_path`, `access_log_line`, CSP `redact_token_url`, `is_public_path`).
+
+### Decisions & rationale (for the PR + future minions)
+
+1. **Five modules, one concern each:** `reference_checks/form_handler.gleam` (HTTP: classify → dispatch, handlers stay thin), `form_pages.gleam` (Lustre SSR views — split `form_pages.gleam` + `form_question_pages.gleam` if either crosses the 400-line view-module target), `form_copy.gleam` (every referee-facing string, the `application/form_copy.gleam` precedent), `questions.gleam` (the per-slot question registry as pure data: ordered ids, copy keys, option vocabs, draft keys, pre-fill bindings — the single source the views, validation, and resume logic all read), plus the four SQL files. Rejected: handler+views in one module (the 200/400-line targets); rejected: questions inline in views (validation and resume would need a second copy).
+2. **`?q=<question-id>` deep links.** Resume = render the first unanswered question in place at the bare URL; `?q=` renders a specific (answered → pre-filled) question and powers Back/Change navigation. Unknown `q` → first unanswered. POST always 303s (PRG, the house pattern).
+3. **Q1 "No" is a link, not an answer.** UX maps it to the wrong-person path; a saved `identity_confirmed="no"` would poison the draft with a non-answer. The link goes to `/reference/:token/wrong-person` (rc3-4 forward contract).
+4. **Resend re-mints the token (not expiry-extension).** "Send me a new link" is honoured literally: old links die (the expired page's own rationale — "old messages can't be reused"), and the expiry guard makes the endpoint self-rate-limiting (see above). Fresh token via `wisp.random_string(48)`.
+5. **Landing renders only when the draft is empty.** First GET with answers already saved resumes straight into the questions (the reminder copy's promise: "the same link picks up where you left off"). `form_opened_at` stamps on either branch (any live-form GET).
+6. **The as-stated degrade is open-form, not fabricated pre-fill** (matrix above). Never interpolate an absent datum; the question goes open (§5.3's own open forms). Recorded as a docs deviation for the reconciliation pass.
+7. **Silent-drop bot semantics mirror /apply exactly:** honeypot-filled or timing-suspicious answer POSTs 303 to the next question with nothing persisted; PUTs return `200 {"ok":true}` with nothing persisted. No 403, no error copy (an error signal teaches the bot which control fired).
+8. **No PostHog, no consent.js, no apply_analytics.js on `/reference/*`** (AC7). The referee is anonymous and the token must never ride an analytics URL. The head reuses `/static/fonts/fonts.css` + `/static/form.css` only.
+9. **New static asset discipline:** `server/priv/static/reference_form.js` + `!server/priv/static/reference_form.js` in `.gitignore` in the SAME commit (3 prior sightings of whitelisted-ignorant assets deploying as dead script tags). CommonJS-exportable pure internals + `node --test` file (the `form_draft.js` pattern). No build step; no client/ changes.
+10. **New audit event `reference_call_link_resent`.** AD-16's list predates the resend flow; the briefing's AC names the resend audit-logged. Append-only variant addition (compile-enforced mapping; `event_type` is unconstrained TEXT — no migration).
+11. **`_focus_seconds` rides every answer form as a hidden field** (maintained by the JS; `_`-prefixed internals are dropped before persistence — the `draft_handler` convention). rc3-3 never stores it; rc3-4 reads it at submit for `form_session` fraud signals.
+
