+
+### Constraints (RT-specific — APPLY here)
+
+- **No em-dashes in user-facing copy** — pages, question text, JS strings: every string gets a `\u{2014}`-absence test (the `welcome_html_has_no_em_dash_test` precedent).
+- **SSR never requires JS** — the no-JS POST path is a first-class tested path, not a degraded one.
+- **Truthful referee copy, calm brand voice** — no "Error"/"Failed", contractions natural, respect the referee's time (they're doing the applicant a favor).
+- **No `let assert` in production code** (tests only); **no JavaScript FFI**; **no new gleam deps**; explicit `httpc` timeouts if any outbound call is added (the resend path uses rc3-2's already-compliant clients).
+- **Capability-token hygiene:** the token appears ONLY in URLs — never in logs, Sentry messages, audit details, attempt entries, or analytics (there are none). Referee PII stays out of log lines.
+- **`data-testid` on all interactive elements** (house rule; bug-hunt consumes them): pin `reference-landing`, `reference-start`, `reference-question`, `reference-progress`, `reference-option-{value}`, `reference-continue`, `reference-back`, `reference-review`, `reference-submit`, `reference-resend`, `reference-decline-link`, `reference-wrong-person-link`.
+
+12. **Per-question timing floor is 500ms, not the /apply 2s (AC6 adaptation).** The form page renders every question at one load, so a fast first tap legitimately lands inside 2s of the stamp; a 2s floor would silently eat it (the fake-advance drops the answer). Answer POST/PUTs keep every fail-closed branch (missing / unparseable / future / >7d) with a 500ms scripted-replay floor; the single-action resend POST keeps the full 2s `is_timing_suspicious` unchanged. Flagged for Perkins.
+13. **`{question, fields:{...}}` PUT payload** — the JS normalizes form fields into a string dict so the no-JS POST and the autosave PUT share ONE validator. `_`-prefixed internals ride the payload (honeypot/timing checks) and never persist.
